description:
## Defect

`skills/re-frame2/patterns/websocket.md` teaches a shortened connection machine. Its `:failed` state (about lines 207-209 at trunk 1ac8076c8a) binds only `:ws/connect` (via `:record-connection-opts`) and `:ws/rotate-cred`. It is missing four bindings:
- no `:ws/send` / `:ws/request` enqueue;
- no `:ws/disconnect`;
- no record-only `:ws/subscribe`;
- its manual `:ws/connect` does not zero the retry counter (the example and spec use `:record-and-reset` there).

The leaf's own prose (about line 237, "bind the record-only action on `:active` AND on `:disconnected`, `:reconnecting` and `:failed`") and `spec/Pattern-WebSocket.md:58` both say `:reconnecting` and `:failed` sit OUTSIDE `:active`, so they inherit none of its doors and must each carry their own. So the leaf's code contradicts its own paragraph.

The offline-queue fix (rf2-3fc89f.29) reached the example and the spec but never this leaf. The rf2-3x7nj.41.2 worker (PR #10340) found it and left it alone because it was outside that item. The leaf's machine binds `:ws/subscribe` nowhere.

## Why it matters

This leaf is AI-facing teaching material. An agent copying its machine ships the exact hole the spec warns about: messages and subscribes issued while `:failed` are unhandled events, in the state a user is most likely to be sitting in.

## Correction

Bring the leaf's shortened machine into line with `spec/Pattern-WebSocket.md`'s worked machine for the sibling states. That means `:failed` and `:reconnecting` each carry:
- `:ws/send` (and `:ws/request`, if the leaf models it at all) enqueue;
- `:ws/disconnect`;
- record-only `:ws/subscribe`;
- the retry-zeroing manual connect.

Keep the leaf SHORT. It may stay a sketch, but it must not contradict its own prose or the spec. If it deliberately omits a door for brevity, it must say so in one line rather than silently.

## Decision needed

No.

